/*******************************************************************************
 * CHIP:  BCMI_QUADRA28
 * REGISTER:  PCS_OPTICS_DIGITAL_CONTROL
 * BLOCKS:   TOP_REGS1LN_TOP_BLOCK
 * REGADDR:  0xc808
 * DEVAD:    1
 * DESC:     PCS Optics Digital Control Register
 * RESETVAL: 0x800 (2048)
 * ACCESS:   R/W
 * FIELDS:
 *     LED_CONTROL      Bicolor mode LED control bits for GPIO(1:0).  Which color LED (if any) gets driven is determined by the 'led_color_sel' field:00 :  LED is off (hardware control enabled if led_color_sel = 2'b00 also).01 :  LED is on.10 :  LED is flashing at 1.0Hz rate.11 :  LED is flashing at 2.0Hz rate.
 *     LED_COLOR_SEL    Bicolor mode LED color selection:00 :  None. (hardware control enabled if led_control = 2'b00 also).01 :  Drive Green LED.10 :  Drive Orange LED.11 :  Drive Green and Orange LEDs.  (Simultaneously if three-leaded LED and 'led_control' = 01;  Alternately if 'led_control' = 1x)
 *     GPIO_SEL         Legacy Mode control bits for GPIO(1:0):00X :Normal mode for GPIO(1:0).In/out controlled by register 1.C80E.010 :GPIO(1)=1  Blink for TX Packets Detected.GPIO(0)=1  Blink for RX Packets Detected.011 :GPIO(1)=1  Blink for TX Packets Detected,otherwise Light-ON forLink on System Rx.GPIO(0)=1  Blink for RX Packets Detected,otherwise Light-ON forLink on Line Rx.10X :GPIO(1)=0  Line-side Link Acquired.GPIO(0)=0  System-side Link Acquired.110 :GPIO(1)=0  TX and/or Rx Packets Detected.GPIO(0)=0  Line-side Link Acquired.111 :GPIO(1)=0  TX and/or Rx Packets Detected.GPIO(0)=0  System-side Link Acquired.Notes:The LEDs blink when Tx/Rx packets are detected.  The rate is about 8x/sec for 10G packets and about 3.5x/sec for 1G packets and has a 50% duty "cycle.
 *     LED_MODE_SEL     Selects how GPIO(1:0) drives the LED(s):0 :  Legacy Mode -- In this mode, GPIO(1:0) function separately as either normal register-driven push-pull I/Os or as open-drain single-color LED drivers.  They are configured by the gpio_sel field.1 :  Bicolor Mode -- In this mode, GPIO(1:0) are standard push-pull outputs and function together as a single bicolor LED driver. They are configured by the led_control, led_color_sel, and led_output_invert fields.  There is also a hardware control mode in which the bicolor LED is controlled by the MOD_ABS and LinkDown signals:LED off at reset and when MOD_ABS = 1.LED Green when link is up.LED Orange if neither of the above.Hardware control is only enabled when both the led_control and led_color_sel fields are set to zero.  Setting either of these fields to nonzero values disables the hardware control, thus the state of the bicolor LED will be determined only by the register fields.Note:  The following LED configurations are supported in Bicolor Mode:(1) One two-leaded bicolor LED connected across GPIO(1:0) with a resistor in series.  Connect GPIO(0) to the anode of the Green LED and GPIO(1) to the anode of the Orange LED.  The cathode connections are implied to be the opposite of the above.(2) One three-leaded bicolor LED with common cathodes connected through a resistor to ground.  Connect GPIO(0) to the anode of the Green LED and GPIO(1) to the anode of the Orange LED.(3) One three-leaded bicolor LED with common anodes connected through a resistor to VDD.  Connect GPIO(0) to the cathode of the Green LED and GPIO(1) to the cathode of the Orange LED.  The 'led_output_invert' bit must be set for this configuration.
 *     LED_OUTPUT_INVERT Inverts the LED output for Bicolor mode only.This allows GPIO(1:0) to drive a three-leaded LED with common anodes connected through a resistor to "VDD.  It also allows a swap of the green and orangeLEDs in the two-leaded bicolor device.  For Legacy Mode, the LED output is always inverted, due to the open-drain GPIO(1:0) configuration.
 *     FORCE_LKDTCMU    = 1 Do not force Low Power modeWhen PMD CMU Loss Of Lock= 0 Force Low Power Mode whenPMD CMU Loss Of Lock
 *     EXT_FLT_EN       1= allow external fault status pins toset alarm status in XEPAK TX/RX alarm registers.0= use DOM registered fault statusin XENPAK TX/RX alarm registersIt also enables TX optical fault to Tx Local fault.
 *     PCS_DIG_PWRDOWN  1 = Digital PCS Power Save Mode;terminate RX/TX clocksQ28 N defeatured
 *     FAULT_MODE       includes rx efifo overflow in xgxs rx local fault
 *
 ******************************************************************************/
