/*******************************************************************************
 * CHIP:  BCMI_QUADRA28
 * REGISTER:  SPI_PORT_CONTROL_STATUS
 * BLOCKS:   TOP_REGS1LN_TOP_BLOCK
 * REGADDR:  0xc848
 * DEVAD:    1
 * DESC:     alternative general purpose register
 * RESETVAL: 0xfc49 (64585)
 * ACCESS:   R/W
 * FIELDS:
 *     GP_POR_CTL_0     General purporse control register reset only by HW PORthis is a broadcast type register
 *     SPA_BYPASS       Spi bypass
 *     SPI_PORT_EN      Channel Micro would SET this bit to enable the SPI port pins when spa_en is SET.Micro should clear this bit, once it has finished its SPI transaction for the other Daisy chained SPI ports to download Micro code.this is a broadcast type register
 *     GP_POR_CTL_5_3   General purporse control register reset only by HW PORthis is a broadcast type register
 *     USE_CENTRAL_M51_FOR_DOWNLOAD Use central micro to download the SPI microcode.1 : Use central micro to download into all the micro's SRAM during SPI download.0 : Use individual micro to download their individual microcode.
 *     NUMBER_OF_ADDR_BYTES Number of bytes used to address the download location.0 : Two byte address from where the SPI download will occur.1 : Use three byte start addressing for SPI download.
 *     SPI_DOWNLOAD_START_ADDR Starting address in external SPI EEPROM from where downloadwill start when External SPI download is called for.00-0x0000 starting address, 01-0x8000 starting address,10-0x1_0000 starting address (3 byte address required),11-0x1_8000 starting address (3 byte address required).
 *     SPI_DOWNLOAD_SIZE Number of bytes that will be download from External SPIwhen download from External SPI is called for.00-32k byte download, 01-44k byte download, 10-52k byte, 11-60k byte download.
 *     SPA_EN           1=SPI Port is enabled in Daisy Chain for the channel Micro to use SPI port for the micro-code download.0=Micro should wait for his turn to use the SPI port.this will be 1 for channel 0 and 0 for all other channelsthis is a broadcast type register
 *     SPI_DWLD_DONE    Micro asserts this bit once SPI/MDIO download is over. This bit cannot be cleared by SW RESET to prevent Firmware download from SPI/MDIO in case Channel is globally reset by SW RESET control bits. This bit is also used to enable the SPI port of the following channels for Daisy channing SPI port pins.<b>This bit is reset only by HW POR. However Micro can write this bit.</b>this is a broadcast type register
 *     SPI_BOOT         Reflects the status of SER_BOOT pin at HW POR.<b>Will be updated 1 clock after reset depending on the mode of the chip.</b>1= Micro should download firmware from external SPI EEPROM/MDIO at reset.0= Micro should use internal ROM for firmware.<b>Note: This bit is reset only by HW POR. However Micro can write this bit.</b>this is a broadcast type register
 *     SPI_PORT_USED    Reflects the status of SPI DOWNLD Mode.<b>Will be updated 1 clock after reset depending on the mode of the chip.</b>1=SPI Port used for mCode download.0= MDIO Port used for mCode download.this is a broadcast type register
 *
 ******************************************************************************/
